WEBVTT

00:00.840 --> 00:04.480
You seem to be an observant person.

00:04.480 --> 00:06.880
I suppose you must look
at things very carefully.

00:07.890 --> 00:13.240
<i>Mister Qifrey might know something 
about that flash of light.</i>

00:13.910 --> 00:16.620
Hey, Mister Qifrey...

00:17.130 --> 00:20.810
There's a question I wanted to ask you.

00:26.230 --> 00:27.620
Well...

00:28.260 --> 00:29.880
That's fantastic!

00:30.720 --> 00:33.200
I'm happy to answer 
whatever questions you have!

00:33.200 --> 00:36.270
I just love talking to 
people about magic!

00:36.270 --> 00:39.270
Go on, Tartah! What do you want to know?!

00:41.270 --> 00:44.430
<i>I can't tell him it's not 
that kind of question...</i>

00:44.430 --> 00:46.780
<i>The sparkles make it especially awkward!</i>

00:46.780 --> 00:48.040
Excuse me.

00:48.530 --> 00:52.150
You dropped off the girl? 
Please, come inside.

00:56.660 --> 01:00.440
It's a cold brought on by exhaustion.

01:03.130 --> 01:06.730
It appears she hasn't 
slept for quite a while.

01:06.730 --> 01:10.100
She should be fine with good 
meals and sufficient rest.

01:10.520 --> 01:13.650
Let's keep her here tonight, 
just to be safe.

01:14.630 --> 01:16.130
Thank you.

01:16.510 --> 01:18.020
Honestly...

01:18.720 --> 01:22.950
I don't know what kind of training 
you witches put yourselves through,

01:22.950 --> 01:25.060
but she's still just a child.

01:25.060 --> 01:29.300
The adults in her life 
need to be more attentive.

01:34.050 --> 01:35.570
She's right.

01:36.310 --> 01:38.330
I'm sorry, Coco.

01:58.810 --> 02:01.770
I hope that eases the fever a bit.

02:01.770 --> 02:05.930
Why would she work herself 
so hard she collapses?

02:06.800 --> 02:12.020
There are times when our bodies, 
minds, and best efforts fail us.

02:12.700 --> 02:17.150
Coco didn't know anything 
about witches until recently.

02:17.480 --> 02:22.450
Even if she acts cheerful, she may 
have been racked with fear deep down.

02:25.680 --> 02:27.490
<i>I didn't realize...</i>

02:27.840 --> 02:30.130
<i>The Outsider everyone's 
been talking about...</i>

02:30.130 --> 02:31.680
<i>Maybe she's—</i>

02:31.680 --> 02:32.840
Tartah.

02:33.390 --> 02:36.280
You said you had a question for me,

02:36.780 --> 02:38.500
but could we discuss it another day?

02:39.760 --> 02:41.470
This isn't the best time.

02:43.420 --> 02:44.640
Right.

02:46.220 --> 02:50.230
I understand. Don't worry about it.

02:52.880 --> 02:54.820
I'd better head home, then.

02:54.820 --> 02:55.760
Thanks.

02:56.290 --> 02:57.210
Take care.

03:11.250 --> 03:16.880
<i>For a second there, 
his gaze was like ice...</i>

03:18.450 --> 03:20.980
<i>Maybe it was just my imagination?</i>

03:22.670 --> 03:23.850
No way!

03:23.850 --> 03:26.920
This ferry is for witches only.

03:26.920 --> 03:30.170
If you live on the island, 
where's your pointed cap?

03:29.770 --> 03:34.690
<b>A Promise in Silver</b>

03:30.170 --> 03:33.590
You can't pass unless you 
can prove you're a witch.

03:33.590 --> 03:34.990
I have it right here...

03:37.740 --> 03:39.480
Huh? It's gone!

03:40.610 --> 03:42.600
I-I crossed this morning, I swear—

03:42.600 --> 03:43.750
Yeah, right!

03:43.750 --> 03:47.390
Tons of little brats try to 
sneak on with that excuse!

03:49.420 --> 03:51.560
Hey, get back here!

03:53.300 --> 03:55.380
<i>I can't get back without my hat.</i>

03:56.050 --> 03:57.300
<i>I have to find it!</i>

03:57.860 --> 04:00.550
Her breathing has settled.

04:03.710 --> 04:06.560
She should feel better if 
she can rest well like this.

04:07.110 --> 04:08.430
I'm glad.

04:08.970 --> 04:10.310
And I must say...

04:10.800 --> 04:14.290
You've made this room so nice and cool.

04:14.290 --> 04:16.560
Isn't magic amazing?

04:16.560 --> 04:18.690
You doctors are amazing, too.

04:19.090 --> 04:22.200
Magic can't cure disease, 
so this is the best I can do.

04:22.200 --> 04:25.540
But it still helps with recovery, right?

04:25.540 --> 04:28.170
I wish we could have this in our toolbox.

04:31.460 --> 04:32.820
I'm sure.

04:34.460 --> 04:35.960
Is there a doctor here?!

04:36.570 --> 04:38.870
The bar to the north caught fire!

04:40.470 --> 04:42.140
We're trying to save the injured,

04:42.140 --> 04:44.820
but they're all so drunk, 
it's hard to move them...

04:47.220 --> 04:50.360
Are you a witch?! And you use water?

04:50.360 --> 04:51.730
Perfect!

04:52.080 --> 04:54.410
Come and help us put out the fire!

04:54.410 --> 04:56.980
You witches help people 
in trouble, don't you?!

04:56.980 --> 04:59.700
E-Excuse me! I can't!

04:59.700 --> 05:01.600
I have to stay here!

05:01.600 --> 05:03.060
It's okay.

05:03.780 --> 05:07.370
You can leave. 
That's a witch's job, right?

05:10.380 --> 05:12.620
All right. I'll be back soon.

05:13.140 --> 05:14.900
Get some good rest.

05:16.320 --> 05:17.890
I'm on my way.

05:17.890 --> 05:19.270
Thank you!

05:19.270 --> 05:20.890
How bad is the fire?

05:20.890 --> 05:25.350
It was still small when I left, 
but we'd better hurry!

05:27.810 --> 05:29.480
<i>I was putting on a brave front.</i>

05:30.120 --> 05:33.890
<i>I'm actually scared to be alone.</i>

05:39.210 --> 05:42.040
<i>I searched everywhere 
and couldn't find it.</i>

05:42.040 --> 05:44.090
<i>This is the only place left—</i>

05:42.930 --> 05:44.090
Let's go!

05:47.790 --> 05:50.360
Excuse me...

06:04.280 --> 06:06.190
Is my hat...

06:07.180 --> 06:08.240
There it is!

06:11.560 --> 06:14.720
Thank goodness. Now I can get back.

06:22.200 --> 06:23.620
She's sleeping fitfully...

06:25.650 --> 06:28.080
H-Hey. You okay?

06:30.740 --> 06:33.060
Tartah?

06:34.510 --> 06:37.430
You startled me. What are you—

06:38.890 --> 06:40.460
You okay?

06:41.340 --> 06:43.590
Looks like your cold's gotten worse.

06:44.120 --> 06:46.840
Isn't anyone here?

06:47.560 --> 06:49.950
There's got to be a 
doctor somewhere, right?

06:49.950 --> 06:51.220
Where's Mister Qifrey?

06:51.620 --> 06:54.700
There was a fire up north, 
so they all went to help.

06:55.920 --> 06:58.270
So that's why they were 
running around out there...

06:58.270 --> 07:00.690
When are they gonna be back?

07:00.690 --> 07:02.990
I could go get someone...

07:07.420 --> 07:09.430
There must be something I can do.

07:09.770 --> 07:12.080
Medicine to bring the fever down?

07:12.580 --> 07:14.670
Remember tranquileaf?

07:14.670 --> 07:16.150
The stuff I used before.

07:16.550 --> 07:19.590
It helps with fever and cough, too.

07:19.590 --> 07:22.290
It's gotta be somewhere nearby...

07:32.170 --> 07:34.640
<i>There aren't any labels...</i>

07:35.090 --> 07:38.200
<i>No way! Who doesn't 
label their medicines?!</i>

07:38.200 --> 07:41.000
<i>What if you mixed them up? Why?!</i>

07:42.690 --> 07:45.740
<i>I think some are darker than others...</i>

07:46.230 --> 07:49.600
<i>Can other people just tell them 
all apart by their color?</i>

07:52.970 --> 07:54.700
Here I go again.

07:55.370 --> 08:00.730
People assume everyone sees 
the world the same way they do.

08:01.510 --> 08:03.140
Silverwash, eh?

08:03.140 --> 08:06.520
He won't be able to use complex 
spells with magic dyes, then.

08:06.520 --> 08:09.620
He'll never make it far 
as a magic stationer, either.

08:09.620 --> 08:12.170
It's not so bad when he's a child, but...

08:12.170 --> 08:14.430
Good thing he's good at carving pens.

08:16.510 --> 08:21.040
There are things that
some people just can't do.

08:21.040 --> 08:23.620
So just stick with the things you <i>can</i> do.

08:24.870 --> 08:26.240
Damn it.

08:27.030 --> 08:30.190
<i>Components in magic dyes are 
often used in medicine, as well.</i>

08:30.190 --> 08:33.500
<i>If I knew what was what, 
I'd know just what they can do...</i>

08:33.840 --> 08:36.120
<i>But when push comes 
to shove, I'm helpless.</i>

08:36.960 --> 08:40.510
<i>In this world where 
everything's silver...</i>

08:40.860 --> 08:43.550
<i>I can't even see a way forward.</i>

08:47.380 --> 08:49.660
Tartah...

08:52.520 --> 08:55.160
Sorry. I can't help you.

08:55.160 --> 08:57.610
I know, you're the one 
who's really suffering...

09:01.870 --> 09:03.520
Right. I'll get you some water.

09:05.270 --> 09:07.530
You're thirsty, right?

09:07.530 --> 09:09.450
Here.

09:13.400 --> 09:14.660
Thanks.

09:18.600 --> 09:20.660
<i>A Vapor Bubble...</i>

09:20.660 --> 09:26.090
<i>That's right. Grandpa always 
uses one when he's making ink...</i>

09:26.090 --> 09:29.890
<i>Of course! I can use this to channel 
out the liquid from the medicine!</i>

09:30.670 --> 09:33.770
<i>If I extract the water 
it's been dissolved in...</i>

09:33.770 --> 09:35.940
<i>Maybe I can identify 
the original components!</i>

09:38.180 --> 09:40.450
<i>Tranquileaf is used as a powder.</i>

09:40.450 --> 09:42.620
<i>They dry it out and crush it.</i>

09:42.940 --> 09:45.230
<i>So if I look for a powder...</i>

09:46.370 --> 09:48.740
It's not these crystals.

09:49.890 --> 09:52.700
It's not this stuff that 
shines in the moonlight...

09:54.700 --> 09:57.850
It's not this stuff that's still liquid.

09:58.810 --> 10:03.790
It doesn't have a distinct smell, 
so I can rule out the pungent ones...

10:05.820 --> 10:07.710
That leaves...

10:13.810 --> 10:15.540
It leaves three.

10:16.470 --> 10:17.740
Damn it. Damn it!

10:17.740 --> 10:22.500
I came this far, but I can't... 
I can't do anything more.

10:23.560 --> 10:26.310
No... more.

10:30.230 --> 10:31.900
I'm sorry, Coco.

10:33.570 --> 10:37.780
I tried my best, but it's just beyond me.

10:40.030 --> 10:43.300
I don't know why I even got my hopes up.

10:44.010 --> 10:48.500
I knew I couldn't do it. 
I knew that all along.

10:52.230 --> 10:54.080
That's not true.

10:55.280 --> 10:59.260
If you want to do something 
you can't otherwise do,

11:00.330 --> 11:03.270
that's where magic comes in.

11:04.450 --> 11:06.110
You have ink and a pen?

11:06.810 --> 11:10.270
Y-Yeah! There's one I've been carving...

11:31.500 --> 11:32.730
You okay?

11:33.560 --> 11:34.670
Yeah.

11:36.490 --> 11:38.800
What kind of spell are you drawing?

11:39.120 --> 11:42.180
Will it make you feel better?

11:44.310 --> 11:47.810
Not me. Not just me.

11:48.530 --> 11:53.350
It's a spell that will help us both.

11:56.380 --> 11:57.690
Me, too?

11:59.550 --> 12:01.950
A spell that will help me, too?

12:02.390 --> 12:04.450
What kind of spell is it?

12:05.770 --> 12:07.460
This is the Sigil of Earth.

12:07.860 --> 12:11.970
It's a spell that's helped me a lot...

12:11.970 --> 12:14.550
digging tunnels, 
turning rocks into sand...

12:15.250 --> 12:17.150
What good will it do now?

12:18.170 --> 12:20.600
Changing the signs changes the spell.

12:21.180 --> 12:24.520
I drew the Signs of Crushing in 
the inverse of their usual position.

12:25.110 --> 12:28.390
It's usually a spell for turning 
solid things into powder.

12:29.480 --> 12:31.930
So if you invert it...

12:33.320 --> 12:36.610
A spell to turn powdered 
things solid again!

12:36.610 --> 12:37.840
Yes.

12:39.150 --> 12:41.740
So, since you're here...

12:42.240 --> 12:48.120
Since you know what 
the originals all look like...

12:48.760 --> 12:51.400
You can use this to find the answer.

12:54.850 --> 12:55.860
What?

12:57.890 --> 13:00.250
I really can't do it like this.

13:00.250 --> 13:02.170
It's all wobbly and uneven...

13:02.170 --> 13:03.700
Okay, so...

13:04.310 --> 13:07.020
You just need these shapes 
drawn more precisely?

13:07.020 --> 13:10.680
W-With better balance, if possible...

13:11.390 --> 13:15.490
Drawing aside, I'm good at 
seeing the balance in things.

13:16.200 --> 13:18.150
It's what I do all the time.

13:29.040 --> 13:30.040
Hey.

13:30.040 --> 13:32.170
This sign here...

13:32.170 --> 13:36.920
Instead of just top and bottom, 
could I draw it on the sides, too?

13:36.920 --> 13:41.300
A three-dimensional object needs 
to be shaped from all angles.

13:41.630 --> 13:43.410
With the spell as it is,

13:43.410 --> 13:46.430
it's probably losing information 
and failing to form right.

13:46.430 --> 13:49.250
So... I mean, sorry.

13:49.250 --> 13:51.410
I didn't mean to alter your spell for you.

13:51.410 --> 13:53.320
No, that's okay.

13:53.320 --> 13:54.940
It's a basic spell.

13:54.940 --> 13:56.190
And...

13:56.950 --> 13:59.570
If you adjust a spell in 
a way that makes it work,

13:59.570 --> 14:03.070
it becomes your spell, Tartah.

14:06.430 --> 14:07.940
Try it.

14:08.550 --> 14:10.950
Sure. I'll try.

15:12.530 --> 15:13.730
I did it.

15:16.090 --> 15:17.590
I did it!

15:17.590 --> 15:19.610
It was just for a second, but I did it!

15:19.950 --> 15:21.230
I did it!

15:21.230 --> 15:22.780
Yay!

15:22.780 --> 15:25.360
Sorry. Right, the medicine...

15:25.360 --> 15:27.360
Man, close call.

15:27.360 --> 15:30.620
None of these were tranquileaf.

15:30.620 --> 15:33.190
I was so sure it had to be one of them...

15:33.710 --> 15:34.730
Okay!

15:37.120 --> 15:40.420
I'll use this spell to search 
the medicine storage room.

15:40.420 --> 15:42.250
It'll be my key to finding it!

15:55.360 --> 15:57.600
<i>It's like my house.</i>

16:03.850 --> 16:05.030
Thornbark.

16:05.030 --> 16:06.530
Milliflower.

16:06.530 --> 16:08.030
Seabriar.

16:08.030 --> 16:09.280
Sleeping Willow.

16:09.280 --> 16:10.780
Drizzlebee Hive.

16:11.800 --> 16:14.920
<i>I know all these shapes.</i>

16:14.920 --> 16:17.290
<i>It's just like how they're 
drawn in the books!</i>

16:18.200 --> 16:19.540
Amazing!

16:20.890 --> 16:25.660
<i>When I hold this seal up to things, 
it's like the world comes into focus.</i>

16:27.480 --> 16:32.180
<i>Everything I've learned 
is showing me the answer.</i>

16:32.910 --> 16:35.440
<i>Learning to do new things feels so...</i>

16:36.200 --> 16:39.950
<i>so amazingly...</i>

16:42.250 --> 16:43.590
I found it.

16:46.640 --> 16:48.610
This is the tranquileaf.

16:48.610 --> 16:50.410
I've gotta get it back and...

16:50.410 --> 16:53.980
Excuse me! What are you doing in there?

16:56.200 --> 16:58.710
You thought nobody was here?

16:58.710 --> 17:00.650
Ridiculous.

17:00.650 --> 17:04.110
We would never leave 
a hospital abandoned.

17:04.550 --> 17:06.950
And the reason the 
medicines aren't labeled

17:06.950 --> 17:09.340
is so that people 
can't fiddle with them.

17:09.340 --> 17:13.730
You could have given her 
a dangerous medicine.

17:13.730 --> 17:16.970
I'm sorry. I was just so panicked...

17:16.970 --> 17:20.500
It's a good thing to 
care about a friend,

17:20.980 --> 17:23.830
but medicine can be poison 
in the wrong circumstances.

17:23.830 --> 17:26.810
You need the proper knowledge.

17:27.180 --> 17:31.240
Though in this case, 
tranquileaf was the correct choice.

17:31.730 --> 17:34.010
Do you know much about medicines?

17:34.010 --> 17:36.000
Any interest in becoming a doctor?

17:36.000 --> 17:38.670
Actually, I...

17:38.670 --> 17:40.870
Oh, that hat.

17:41.190 --> 17:44.450
You're a witch apprentice, then?

17:50.510 --> 17:52.880
We've gotten all the injured out.

17:53.220 --> 17:55.170
Thank goodness.

17:55.170 --> 17:57.200
I appreciate your support.

17:58.140 --> 18:02.500
The fire's mostly out, 
so can I leave the rest to you?

18:03.300 --> 18:04.650
I'm worried about my apprentice...

18:04.650 --> 18:07.270
Hey, you're not going anywhere!

18:07.270 --> 18:10.280
We still need to clean up the site!

18:10.280 --> 18:15.070
You witches can go "presto, change!" 
and have it done in a flash, right?

18:15.070 --> 18:18.140
I need you leading the work!

18:18.140 --> 18:19.680
Please, mister!

18:19.680 --> 18:23.750
Um, it's really not that easy...

18:24.220 --> 18:26.690
Outsiders don't understand that.

18:27.840 --> 18:31.310
Do not worry. My apprentice 
and I will handle the rest.

18:31.310 --> 18:32.650
Thank you.

18:38.500 --> 18:40.800
<i>It's not easy or simple.</i>

18:41.400 --> 18:42.510
<i>Not a bit.</i>

18:43.820 --> 18:48.310
<i>If it were, we wouldn't have 
to worry or suffer as we do.</i>

19:10.310 --> 19:11.750
My breathing's so much easier!

19:12.640 --> 19:13.760
I'm so glad.

19:13.760 --> 19:16.180
I guess the medicine worked.

19:16.180 --> 19:18.000
Thanks, Tartah.

19:18.890 --> 19:20.010
Well...

19:20.710 --> 19:24.140
Actually, you're the one who helped me.

19:29.470 --> 19:31.400
Witches are amazing, huh?

19:33.970 --> 19:36.150
Witches are amazing, yeah.

19:39.660 --> 19:43.940
I was worried. You were out all night.

19:43.940 --> 19:45.660
Sorry, Grandpa.

19:45.660 --> 19:48.860
Thanks for letting me know, Qifrey.

19:48.860 --> 19:51.720
I'm sure you'd do the same for me.

19:51.720 --> 19:52.920
Oh, right.

19:52.920 --> 19:58.300
Um, I wanted to ask about 
that flash of light I saw...

19:59.070 --> 20:00.290
Flash of light?

20:02.270 --> 20:04.020
Never mind.

20:04.610 --> 20:07.490
You push yourself too hard, you know.

20:07.490 --> 20:09.310
Watch your health, now.

20:09.670 --> 20:13.480
You, too, Mister Nolnoa. 
Look after yourself.

20:10.130 --> 20:13.070
<i>Maybe I imagined it.</i>

20:13.070 --> 20:17.680
<i>I'll have to look into that 
powerful light again on my own.</i>

20:13.480 --> 20:14.810
Goodbye, then.

20:17.680 --> 20:18.660
Tartah.

20:19.380 --> 20:20.570
The ferry's leaving.

20:22.000 --> 20:25.580
Master! I'm sorry to keep you waiting.

20:26.120 --> 20:27.580
Boat's heading out.

20:34.420 --> 20:35.560
Tartah!

20:36.340 --> 20:37.670
See you later!

20:44.750 --> 20:47.090
We should head home, too.

20:47.090 --> 20:48.100
Okay!

20:57.150 --> 20:58.530
Coco!

20:58.530 --> 21:02.160
I'm going to make a pen for you!

21:02.160 --> 21:06.040
Then I'll use my own magic 
to cross this river

21:06.040 --> 21:09.210
and deliver it right to you! I promise!

21:10.990 --> 21:12.040
Okay!

21:17.570 --> 21:19.800
I can't wait to see it!

21:23.090 --> 21:26.420
You two have become close friends, eh?

21:26.750 --> 21:30.310
Yeah. She's amazing.

21:30.310 --> 21:33.990
And I bet she'll become more amazing.

21:37.190 --> 21:41.700
You'll become amazing, too.

21:47.650 --> 21:48.830
I see.

21:48.830 --> 21:52.080
You've been tormented 
by nightmares all this time?

21:52.430 --> 21:54.620
Dreams are difficult to deal with,

21:54.620 --> 21:57.250
and sleeping spells are 
considered forbidden...

21:57.720 --> 22:00.340
Still, let's try to find 
a way to help you.

22:00.730 --> 22:03.320
Necessity is the mother of invention.

22:03.980 --> 22:05.770
Thank you very much.

22:05.770 --> 22:09.220
But I think I'll be okay now.

22:09.570 --> 22:10.860
You're not just being brave?

22:11.300 --> 22:11.890
I'm not.

22:12.520 --> 22:13.390
Because...

22:14.400 --> 22:17.270
I found a ray of hope.

22:18.950 --> 22:22.860
<i>Drawing the signs backwards 
inverts their effect.</i>

22:23.290 --> 22:26.530
<i>Forbidden spells must be the same way.</i>

22:29.460 --> 22:33.040
<i>If I draw inverse signs 
of the seal in that book,</i>

22:33.640 --> 22:37.210
<i>maybe I can reverse the spell 
that turned my mom to stone, too!</i>

22:37.210 --> 22:39.050
Coco!

22:39.050 --> 22:41.530
Hey!

22:43.110 --> 22:44.800
I was so worried!

22:45.190 --> 22:46.860
Is your fever all gone?

22:46.860 --> 22:47.830
Yeah.

22:48.740 --> 22:50.000
I'm so glad!

22:50.000 --> 22:51.310
So very glad!

22:56.960 --> 23:00.820
It seems your gift 
didn't work out very well.

23:02.320 --> 23:07.820
The Pointed Caps aren't all fools 
gone soft from days of peace.

23:08.220 --> 23:10.530
We cannot sit idly by.

23:10.530 --> 23:13.790
We must take further action.

23:13.790 --> 23:17.070
You'll be going next, then?

23:17.540 --> 23:21.580
As an embodiment of forbidden magic...

23:21.980 --> 23:24.100
I certainly intend to.

23:24.920 --> 23:29.170
When an apprentice leaves their 
master's protection during a test...

23:29.800 --> 23:32.840
That is when we must strike.

23:35.390 --> 23:40.060
Episode 11:

23:35.390 --> 23:40.060
The Test in Serpentback Cave
